---
import Funnel from '../layouts/Funnel.astro';
import BrandHeader from '../components/BrandHeader.astro';
import BrandFooter from '../components/BrandFooter.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import '../styles/funnel-v5.css';
const phases=[
  {name:'The Reading',title:'Understand what happened.',body:'Look at a situation you recognize. Write down what happened, what you thought, and what you did.',output:'Put a recent experience into words.'},
  {name:'The Move',title:'Try a different response.',body:'Look at the expectations behind a familiar response and decide what you’d like to try differently.',output:'Decide what you could try next.'},
  {name:'The Hold',title:'Keep working with it.',body:'Try the exercise during your week. Look at what helped, what got in the way, and what you’d change.',output:'Adjust the plan when you need to.'},
];
---
<Funnel title="Pick up where you left off | Protocol 44" description="A personal development program built around guided lessons, audio practices and reflection. Find a starting point and try the first written practice.">
  <BrandHeader page="home" />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="product-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="product-title">
      <div class="product-hero-copy"><h1 id="product-title">Pick up where<br />you <span>left off.</span></h1><p class="hero-intro">You had a plan. Then work, family, or a busy week got in the way. It may still be something you want.</p><p class="hero-description">Protocol 44 is a personal development program about the patterns that make it hard to follow through. Start with a few questions, then try an exercise from the first lesson.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/quiz">Take the quiz <Arrow /></a><p class="button-note">10 questions. Free, with no email needed.</p><a href="#inside" class="hero-secondary">See what’s inside</a></div>
      <figure class="editorial-photo"><img src="/brand/quiet-practice-v5.webp" width="1536" height="1024" alt="A woman writing in a notebook at a kitchen table in afternoon light" fetchpriority="high" /></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="recognition-section wrap" data-motion aria-labelledby="recognition-title"><h2 id="recognition-title">It can be hard<br />to keep going.</h2><div><p class="lead">Maybe you’ve filled a notebook with plans or felt better after a guided audio. A busy week goes by, and you haven’t come back to it.</p><p>Start with a recent example. The first exercise helps you separate what happened from what you told yourself, so you can decide what to do next.</p></div></section>
    <section class="product-inside wrap" id="inside" aria-labelledby="inside-title"><div class="section-heading" data-motion><h2 id="inside-title">How the<br />program works</h2><div><p>We’re developing 22 lessons, each paired with an audio exercise and questions to work through in writing.</p><p>The course has three parts. You can try the first written exercise now while we prepare the full program.</p></div></div><div class="product-phases">{phases.map((p,i)=><article class="product-phase"><div><span class="phase-order" aria-label={`Phase ${i+1}`}>{i+1}</span><h3>{p.name}</h3></div><div><h4>{p.title}</h4><p>{p.body}</p></div><p class="phase-output">{p.output}</p></article>)}</div><p class="availability-note">The full program is in preparation. Explore the first written sample below; enrollment and recordings are not available yet.</p></section>
    <section class="example-section" aria-labelledby="example-title"><div class="wrap example-layout"><div data-motion><h2 id="example-title">Here’s an example.</h2><p>Maya wanted to keep track of her spending. When she missed her Sunday review, she put the notebook away for the rest of the week.</p><p class="example-disclosure">Maya is a fictional example from the first lesson.</p><a href="/vsl#first-practice" class="button button-dark">Try the exercise <Arrow /></a></div><div id="example-story" class="example-workbook"><div class="example-controls" role="group" aria-label="Explore Maya’s example"><button type="button" data-example-step="0" aria-pressed="true">What happened</button><button type="button" data-example-step="1" aria-pressed="false">What she thought</button><button type="button" data-example-step="2" aria-pressed="false">What she could try</button></div><div data-example-panel="0"><h3>She missed her Sunday review.</h3><p>Maya planned ten minutes to review the week’s expenses. A family visit ran late, and she missed her usual time.</p><p class="example-question">Start with what happened.</p></div><div data-example-panel="1" hidden><h3>“I never stick with this.”</h3><p>That is what Maya told herself the next morning. She noticed avoiding the notebook for the rest of the week.</p><p class="example-question">Notice the thought that followed.</p></div><div data-example-panel="2" hidden><h3>Open the notebook.<br />Check one bill.</h3><p>On Monday, Maya can take one small step and schedule the rest of the review separately.</p><p class="example-question">Choose something she could do now.</p></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="fit-section wrap" data-motion><h2>Make it work<br />for your week.</h2><div><p class="lead">You can use the sample whether you’re used to journaling or trying it for the first time. Start with something you feel comfortable writing about.</p><ul class="plain-list"><li>Choose something you’d like to work on.</li><li>Use a recent example you remember.</li><li>Leave a question blank if you’re not sure.</li><li>Come back to your notes after you’ve tried your next step.</li></ul></div></section>
    <section class="faq-section wrap" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><h2 id="faq-title">A few questions<br />you might have</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>What will I get from the quiz?</summary><p>You’ll see a suggested topic to work on, a question to think about, and a link to the first exercise. Your result appears on screen. You won’t need to give us your email.</p></details><details><summary>What if I’ve tried something like this before?</summary><p>Try the sample first. You can read the instructions and fill in the worksheet before deciding whether this approach is useful to you.</p></details><details><summary>What if the result doesn’t feel right?</summary><p>You can change your focus or review your answers. The quiz suggests a topic to explore; it doesn’t tell you who you are.</p></details><details><summary>How will the audio exercises work?</summary><p>They’ll guide you through the ideas from each lesson, with pauses to think and time to write afterward. We’re still preparing the recordings.</p></details><details><summary>Is the full program available?</summary><p>It is still in preparation. The first written sample is available now. The final schedule, access terms and support details will be shared before enrollment opens.</p></details><details><summary>Is this therapy?</summary><p>Protocol 44 is educational self-reflection. It does not provide a clinical assessment or replace professional care. Choose manageable situations for the sample and pause whenever you need.</p></details></div></section>
    <section class="product-close wrap" data-motion><img src="/brand/symbol-ink.svg" alt="" width="90" height="90" /><h2>What would you<br />like to work on?</h2><p>Take the quiz and try the first exercise.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/quiz">Take the quiz <Arrow /></a></section>
  </main><BrandFooter />
  <script>import '../lib/page-motion';</script>
</Funnel>
